From d822256f57b28681529341859e63a78c487d5910 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 22:01:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] shared: close animations-off leaks in View, widgets and
 SystemUI

Several per-frame effects ignore the animator duration scale. With
animations off (ValueAnimator.areAnimatorsEnabled() false):
- View scrollbars hide in one frame instead of a 250 ms fade
- TextView does not start a marquee (static ellipsized text)
- Scroller/OverScroller.startScroll land on the first frame (page keys,
  smooth scrolls, page snaps); flings are unchanged
- Compose QS tile labels do not run basicMarquee
- SystemUI AnimationDrawable icons (download/upload) show their first
  frame instead of a 5 Hz loop, in the status bar and notification rows
- Compose text cursors in Settings (SettingsTheme) and SystemUI
  (PlatformTheme) do not blink (LocalCursorBlinkEnabled)
Behaviour with animations on is unchanged.

Change-Id: I9df91b7d69039a8c208a70ef6966fbaf4318aebc

AnimatedImageView.updateAnim() and onVisibilityChanged() now use shouldAnimate(), so status-bar download/upload icons also stop with animations off (it was added but not called).
